{"zeu/gnumi": {"key": "zeu/gnumi", "head": "†ζεύγνυμι", "html": "<div class=\"cunliffe-sense\">†ζεύγνυμι [ζυγόν.] Infin. ζευγνύμεναι <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"3\" data-line=\"260\">Il. 3.260</a>. ζευγνύ̆μεν Il. 15.120. ζευγνῦμεν Il. 16.145. 3 pl. impf. ζεύγνυον <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"19\" data-line=\"393\">Il. 19.393</a>. ζεύγνυσαν Il. 24.783. 3 sing. aor. ζεῦξε <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"24\" data-line=\"690\">Il. 24.690</a>: <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"6\" data-line=\"253\">Od. 6.253</a>. 3 pl. ἔζευξαν <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"3\" data-line=\"478\">Od. 3.478</a>. ζεῦξαν Il. 24.277: <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"6\" data-line=\"73\">Od. 6.73</a>. 3 sing. subj. ζεύξῃ <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"20\" data-line=\"495\">Il. 20.495</a>. 3 sing. opt. ζεύξειε <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"24\" data-line=\"14\">Il. 24.14</a>. Imp. ζεῦξον <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"15\" data-line=\"47\">Od. 15.47</a>. Pl. ζεύξατε <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"20\" data-line=\"476\">Il. 20.476</a>. Fem. pple. ζεύξασα <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"6\" data-line=\"111\">Od. 6.111</a>. Infin. ζεῦξαι <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"23\" data-line=\"130\">Il. 23.130</a>. Pres. infin. mid. ζεύγνυσθαι <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"23\" data-line=\"245\">Od. 23.245</a>. 3 dual impf. ζευγνύσθην <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"24\" data-line=\"281\">Il. 24.281</a>. 3 pl. (ἐ)ζεύγνυντο <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"3\" data-line=\"492\">Od. 3.492</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"15\" data-line=\"145\">Od. 15.145</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"15\" data-line=\"190\">190</a>. Nom. pl. fem. pf. pple. pass. ἐζευγμέναι <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"18\" data-line=\"276\">Il. 18.276</a>. (ὑπο-.) 1 To yoke (horses, mules, or oxen) <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"3\" data-line=\"260\">Il. 3.260</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"15\" data-line=\"120\">Il. 15.120</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"16\" data-line=\"145\">Il. 16.145</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"19\" data-line=\"393\">Il. 19.393</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"20\" data-line=\"495\">Il. 20.495</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"23\" data-line=\"130\">Il. 23.130</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"24\" data-line=\"14\">Il. 24.14</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"24\" data-line=\"277\">277</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"24\" data-line=\"690\">690</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"24\" data-line=\"783\">783</a>: <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"3\" data-line=\"476\">Od. 3.476</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"3\" data-line=\"478\">478</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"6\" data-line=\"73\">Od. 6.73</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"6\" data-line=\"111\">111</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"6\" data-line=\"253\">253</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"15\" data-line=\"47\">Od. 15.47</a>. In mid., to have one&#x27;s beasts yoked: τὼ ζευγνύσθην Il. 24.281. To have (one&#x27;s beasts) yoked: ἵππους ἐζεύγνυντο Od. 3.492 = <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"15\" data-line=\"145\">Od. 15.145 =</a> <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"15\" data-line=\"190\">190. Cf</a>. <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"23\" data-line=\"245\">Od. 23.245</a>. 2 To join together, secure together in position: σανίδες ἐζευγμέναι <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"18\" data-line=\"276\">Il. 18.276</a>.</div>", "src": "lex"}, "zw/nnumi": {"key": "zw/nnumi", "head": "ζώννυμι", "html": "<div class=\"cunliffe-sense\">ζώννυμι Nom. pl. masc. aor. pple. ζώσαντες <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"18\" data-line=\"76\">Od. 18.76</a>. App. as 3 pl. pres. subj. mid. ζώννυνται Od. 24.89. 3 sing. pa. iterative ζωννύσκετο <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"5\" data-line=\"857\">Il. 5.857</a>. 3 sing. aor. ζώσατο <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"14\" data-line=\"181\">Il. 14.181</a>: <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"18\" data-line=\"67\">Od. 18.67</a>. Imp. ζῶσαι <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"18\" data-line=\"30\">Od. 18.30</a>. Nom. dual masc. pple. ζωσαμένω <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"23\" data-line=\"685\">Il. 23.685</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"23\" data-line=\"710\">710</a>. 1 To gird up (a person) for action <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"18\" data-line=\"76\">Od. 18.76</a>. 2 In mid. a To gird oneself: ζώσατο ζώνῃ Il. 14.181 (v.l. ζώνην, put on her . . .). b To gird oneself up for action: ζώννυσθαι ἄνωγεν Il. 11.15. Cf. <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"5\" data-line=\"857\">Il. 5.857</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"10\" data-line=\"78\">Il. 10.78</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"23\" data-line=\"685\">Il. 23.685</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"23\" data-line=\"710\">710</a>: <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"18\" data-line=\"30\">Od. 18.30</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"18\" data-line=\"67\">67</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"24\" data-line=\"89\">Od. 24.89</a>. With acc. of what is girded on: κέλευσε χαλκὸν ζώννυσθαι <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"23\" data-line=\"130\">Il. 23.130</a> (cf. v.l. under a and μίτρην, v.l. for μίτρῃ <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"5\" data-line=\"857\">Il. 5.857</a>).</div>", "src": "lex"}, "zeu/glh": {"key": "zeu/glh", "head": "ζεύγλη", "html": "<div class=\"cunliffe-sense\">ζεύγλη -ης, ἡ [ζευγ-, ζεύγνυμι.] A cushion fastened under the yoke to prevent chafing, a yoke-cushion <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"17\" data-line=\"440\">Il. 17.440</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"19\" data-line=\"406\">Il. 19.406</a>.</div>", "src": "lex"}, "zwh/": {"key": "zwh/", "head": "ζωή", "html": "<div class=\"cunliffe-sense\">ζωή -ῆς, ἡ [ζώω.] Life; hence, the means of living, means, substance <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"14\" data-line=\"96\">Od. 14.96</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"14\" data-line=\"208\">208</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"16\" data-line=\"429\">Od. 16.429</a>.</div>", "src": "lex"}, "zatrefh/s": {"key": "zatrefh/s", "head": "ζατρεφής", "html": "<div class=\"cunliffe-sense\">ζατρεφής [ζα- + τρέφω.] Well-nourished, goodly <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"4\" data-line=\"451\">Od. 4.451</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"14\" data-line=\"19\">Od. 14.19</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"14\" data-line=\"106\">106</a>. Of, prepared from, such an animal: σάκος ταύρων ζατρεφέων <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"7\" data-line=\"223\">Il. 7.223</a>.</div>", "src": "lex"}, "zo/fos": {"key": "zo/fos", "head": "ζόφος", "html": "<div class=\"cunliffe-sense\">ζόφος -ου, ὁ. Darkness, gloom. 1 The gloom of the nether world: ἀναστήσονται ὑπὸ ζόφου Il. 21.56. Cf. <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"23\" data-line=\"51\">Il. 23.51</a>: <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"11\" data-line=\"57\">Od. 11.57</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"11\" data-line=\"155\">155</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"20\" data-line=\"356\">Od. 20.356</a>. The nether world: αΐδης ἔλαχε ζόφον Il. 15.191. 2 The gloom into which the sun appears to set <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"3\" data-line=\"335\">Od. 3.335</a>. The region of darkness, the quarter of the setting sun, the west: σπέος πρὸς ζόφον εἰς Ἔρεβος τετραμμένον (i.e., app., facing west with an internal downward direction) <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"12\" data-line=\"81\">Od. 12.81</a>. Contrasted with ἠώς Od. 10.190. With ἠώς τʼ ἠέλιός τε Il. 12.240: <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"9\" data-line=\"26\">Od. 9.26</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"13\" data-line=\"241\">Od. 13.241</a>.</div>", "src": "lex"}, "zeu=gos": {"key": "zeu=gos", "head": "ζεῦγος", "html": "<div class=\"cunliffe-sense\">ζεῦγος τό [ζεύγνυμι.] A team of draught-animals: ζεύγεα ἐλάστρεον <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"18\" data-line=\"543\">Il. 18.543</a>.</div>", "src": "lex"}, "ze/w": {"key": "ze/w", "head": "ζέω", "html": "<div class=\"cunliffe-sense\">ζέω 3 sing. aor. ζέσσε <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"18\" data-line=\"349\">Il. 18.349</a>: <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"10\" data-line=\"360\">Od. 10.360</a>. Of water, to boil up, boil: ἐπεὶ ζέσσεν ὕδωρ (had come to the boil) Il. 18.349: = <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"10\" data-line=\"360\">Od. 10.360</a>. Of the containing caldron: ὡς λέβης ζεῖ ἔνδον Il. 21.362. Of the waters of a river exposed to fire <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"21\" data-line=\"365\">Il. 21.365</a>.</div>", "src": "lex"}, "zw/w": {"key": "zw/w", "head": "ζώω", "html": "<div class=\"cunliffe-sense\">ζώω Contr. genit. sing. masc. pres. pple. ζῶντος <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"1\" data-line=\"88\">Il. 1.88</a>. 1 To be alive, live: ζώειν φασὶ μενοίτιον Il. 16.14. Cf. <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"1\" data-line=\"88\">Il. 1.88</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"5\" data-line=\"157\">Il. 5.157</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"18\" data-line=\"10\">Il. 18.10</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"19\" data-line=\"327\">Il. 19.327</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"22\" data-line=\"49\">Il. 22.49, etc</a>.: <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"2\" data-line=\"132\">Od. 2.132</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"3\" data-line=\"354\">Od. 3.354</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"11\" data-line=\"303\">Od. 11.303</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"12\" data-line=\"21\">Od. 12.21</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"17\" data-line=\"391\">Od. 17.391</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"22\" data-line=\"38\">Od. 22.38, etc</a>. 2 Absol. in pres. pple. pl., the living, men: ἀγαυότατον ζωόντων Od. 15.229. Cf. <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"10\" data-line=\"72\">Od. 10.72</a>. 3 To pass a life or existence of a specified kind: θεοὶ ῥεῖα ζώοντες Il. 6.138. Cf. <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"24\" data-line=\"526\">Il. 24.526</a>: θεοὶ ὄλβια δοῖεν ζωέμεναι (prosperity that they may pass their lives therein) Od. 7.149. Cf. <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"4\" data-line=\"805\">Od. 4.805</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"5\" data-line=\"122\">Od. 5.122</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"17\" data-line=\"423\">Od. 17.423 =</a> <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"19\" data-line=\"79\">Od. 19.79</a>. With cognate acc.: ζώεις ἀγαθὸν βίον <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"15\" data-line=\"491\">Od. 15.491</a>.</div>", "src": "lex"}, "za/kunqos": {"key": "za/kunqos", "head": "Ζάκυνθος", "html": "<div class=\"cunliffe-sense\">Ζάκυνθος (ὑλήεις, ὑλήεσσα ). The mod. Zante. An island forming part of the realm of Odysseus <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"2\" data-line=\"634\">Il. 2.634</a>. In Od. associated with Doulichium, Same and Ithaca <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"1\" data-line=\"246\">Od. 1.246</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"9\" data-line=\"24\">Od. 9.24</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"16\" data-line=\"123\">Od. 16.123</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"16\" data-line=\"250\">250</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"19\" data-line=\"131\">Od. 19.131</a>.</div>", "src": "hompers"}, "zugo/desmon": {"key": "zugo/desmon", "head": "ζυγόδεσμον", "html": "<div class=\"cunliffe-sense\">ζυγόδεσμον τό [ζυγόν + δεσμός.] A yoke-fastening, the rope or thong by which the yoke was secured to the pole <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"24\" data-line=\"270\">Il. 24.270</a>.</div>", "src": "lex"}, "zwro/s": {"key": "zwro/s", "head": "ζωρός", "html": "<div class=\"cunliffe-sense\">ζωρός Of wine, strong, unmixed. In comp.: κρητῆρα ζωρότερον κέραιε <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"9\" data-line=\"203\">Il. 9.203</a>.</div>", "src": "lex"}, "zwsth/r": {"key": "zwsth/r", "head": "ζωστήρ", "html": "<div class=\"cunliffe-sense\">ζωστήρ -ῆρος, ὁ [ζωσ-, ζώννυμι.] 1 A warrior&#x27;s belt <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"4\" data-line=\"132\">Il. 4.132</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"4\" data-line=\"134\">134</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"4\" data-line=\"135\">135</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"4\" data-line=\"186\">186</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"4\" data-line=\"213\">213</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"4\" data-line=\"215\">215</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"5\" data-line=\"539\">Il. 5.539</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"5\" data-line=\"615\">615</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"6\" data-line=\"219\">Il. 6.219</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"7\" data-line=\"305\">Il. 7.305</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"10\" data-line=\"77\">Il. 10.77</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"11\" data-line=\"236\">Il. 11.236</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"12\" data-line=\"189\">Il. 12.189</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"17\" data-line=\"519\">Il. 17.519</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"17\" data-line=\"578\">578</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"20\" data-line=\"414\">Il. 20.414</a>. 2 A belt or girdle worn in ordinary life <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"14\" data-line=\"72\">Od. 14.72</a>.</div>", "src": "lex"}, "zw=ma": {"key": "zw=ma", "head": "ζῶμα", "html": "<div class=\"cunliffe-sense\">ζῶμα τό [ζώννυμι. That which is girded about one.] 1 A waist-cloth or apron, prob. of leather, worn in warfare <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"4\" data-line=\"187\">Il. 4.187</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"4\" data-line=\"216\">216</a>: <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"14\" data-line=\"482\">Od. 14.482</a>. 2 Something of the same kind, but doubtless of lighter material, worn in an athletic contest <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"23\" data-line=\"683\">Il. 23.683</a>.</div>", "src": "lex"}, "zaxrhh/s": {"key": "zaxrhh/s", "head": "ζαχρηής", "html": "<div class=\"cunliffe-sense\">ζαχρηής ζαχρειής [ζα- (perh.) χράω2. Fierce in attack.] 1 Furious or formidable in fight <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"12\" data-line=\"347\">Il. 12.347 =</a> <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"12\" data-line=\"360\">360</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"13\" data-line=\"684\">Il. 13.684</a>. 2 Of winds, furious, blustering <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"5\" data-line=\"525\">Il. 5.525</a>.</div>", "src": "lex"}, "zwa/gria": {"key": "zwa/gria", "head": "ζωάγρια", "html": "<div class=\"cunliffe-sense\">ζωάγρια τά [ζωγρέω1. App. orig. the price paid for sparing a prisoner&#x27;s life.] The price of one&#x27;s life, a reward for preserving one&#x27;s life by care or help <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"18\" data-line=\"407\">Il. 18.407</a>: <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"8\" data-line=\"462\">Od. 8.462</a>.</div>", "src": "lex"}, "zw/nh": {"key": "zw/nh", "head": "ζώνη", "html": "<div class=\"cunliffe-sense\">ζώνη -ης, ἡ [ζώννυμι.] 1 A girdle worn by a goddess or a woman: ζώσατο ζώνῃ Il. 14.181. Cf. <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"5\" data-line=\"231\">Od. 5.231 =</a> <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"10\" data-line=\"544\">Od. 10.544</a>. Fig.: λῦσε παρθενίην ζώνην (her maiden girdle) Od. 11.245. 2 The waist or loins of a man <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"2\" data-line=\"479\">Il. 2.479</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"11\" data-line=\"234\">Il. 11.234</a>.</div>", "src": "lex"}, "zw/s": {"key": "zw/s", "head": "ζώς", "html": "<div class=\"cunliffe-sense\">ζώς Acc. ζών. = ζωός 1 <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"5\" data-line=\"887\">Il. 5.887</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"16\" data-line=\"445\">Il. 16.445</a>.</div>", "src": "lex"}, "ze/furos": {"key": "ze/furos", "head": "Ζέφυρος", "html": "<div class=\"cunliffe-sense\">Ζέφυρος -ου, ὁ. The west wind <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"2\" data-line=\"147\">Il. 2.147</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"4\" data-line=\"276\">Il. 4.276</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"4\" data-line=\"423\">423</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"7\" data-line=\"63\">Il. 7.63</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"9\" data-line=\"5\">Il. 9.5</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"11\" data-line=\"305\">Il. 11.305</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"19\" data-line=\"415\">Il. 19.415</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"21\" data-line=\"334\">Il. 21.334</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"23\" data-line=\"195\">Il. 23.195</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"23\" data-line=\"200\">200</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"23\" data-line=\"208\">208</a>: <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"2\" data-line=\"421\">Od. 2.421</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"4\" data-line=\"402\">Od. 4.402</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"4\" data-line=\"567\">567</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"5\" data-line=\"295\">Od. 5.295</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"5\" data-line=\"332\">332</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"10\" data-line=\"25\">Od. 10.25</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"12\" data-line=\"289\">Od. 12.289</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"12\" data-line=\"408\">408</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"12\" data-line=\"426\">426</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"14\" data-line=\"458\">Od. 14.458</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"19\" data-line=\"206\">Od. 19.206</a>. Joined with ἄνεμος <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"16\" data-line=\"150\">Il. 16.150</a>.</div>", "src": "lex"}, "zwo/s": {"key": "zwo/s", "head": "ζωός", "html": "<div class=\"cunliffe-sense\">ζωός -ή [ζώω.] 1 Alive, living: ζωόν τε καὶ ἀρτεμέα Il. 5.515, ζωὸν ἕλεν (took prisoner) Il. 6.38. Cf. <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"2\" data-line=\"699\">Il. 2.699</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"6\" data-line=\"50\">Il. 6.50</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"12\" data-line=\"10\">Il. 12.10</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"18\" data-line=\"418\">Il. 18.418</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"23\" data-line=\"77\">Il. 23.77, etc</a>.: <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"1\" data-line=\"197\">Od. 1.197</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"3\" data-line=\"256\">Od. 3.256</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"11\" data-line=\"78\">Od. 11.78</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"11\" data-line=\"78\">Od. 11.78</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"11\" data-line=\"86\">86</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"14\" data-line=\"272\">Od. 14.272</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"19\" data-line=\"272\">Od. 19.272</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"23\" data-line=\"55\">Od. 23.55, etc</a>. 2 Absol. in pl. a The living, those not slain: ζωοὺς σάω Il. 21.238. b Those yet in life: χαλεπὸν τάδε ζωοῖσιν ὁρᾶσθαι Od. 11.156. c The living, men: ὄφρʼ ἂν ζωοῖσιν μετέω Il. 22.388. Cf. <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"23\" data-line=\"47\">Il. 23.47</a>: <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"10\" data-line=\"52\">Od. 10.52</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"14\" data-line=\"487\">Od. 14.487</a>.</div>", "src": "lex"}, "zeu/s": {"key": "zeu/s", "head": "Ζεύς", "html": "<div class=\"cunliffe-sense\">Ζεύς Genit. Ζηνός <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"4\" data-line=\"408\">408</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"11\" data-line=\"795\">Il. 11.795</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"12\" data-line=\"235\">Il. 12.235</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"13\" data-line=\"449\">Il. 13.449, etc</a>. : <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"1\" data-line=\"27\">Od. 1.27</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"2\" data-line=\"68\">Od. 2.68</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"4\" data-line=\"74\">Od. 4.74, etc</a>. Dat. Ζηνί <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"2\" data-line=\"49\">49</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"4\" data-line=\"1\">Il. 4.1</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"7\" data-line=\"443\">Il. 7.443, etc</a>.: <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"4\" data-line=\"78\">Od. 4.78</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"9\" data-line=\"552\">Od. 9.552</a>. Acc. Ζῆνα <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"5\" data-line=\"756\">756</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"8\" data-line=\"22\">Il. 8.22</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"14\" data-line=\"157\">Il. 14.157, etc</a>.: <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"20\" data-line=\"339\">Od. 20.339</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"24\" data-line=\"472\">Od. 24.472</a>. Ζῆν <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"8\" data-line=\"206\">206</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"14\" data-line=\"265\">Il. 14.265</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"24\" data-line=\"331\">Il. 24.331</a>. Voc. Ζεῦ <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"1\" data-line=\"503\">503</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"2\" data-line=\"371\">Il. 2.371</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"3\" data-line=\"298\">Il. 3.298</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"5\" data-line=\"421\">Il. 5.421, etc</a>.: <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"1\" data-line=\"62\">Od. 1.62</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"4\" data-line=\"341\">Od. 4.341</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"5\" data-line=\"7\">Od. 5.7</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"7\" data-line=\"331\">Od. 7.331, etc</a>. Genit. Διός <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"1\" data-line=\"5\">5</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"2\" data-line=\"26\">Il. 2.26</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"3\" data-line=\"107\">Il. 3.107</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"4\" data-line=\"128\">Il. 4.128, etc</a>.: <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"1\" data-line=\"10\">Od. 1.10</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"2\" data-line=\"296\">Od. 2.296</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"3\" data-line=\"42\">Od. 3.42</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"4\" data-line=\"27\">Od. 4.27, etc</a>. Dat. Διί <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"1\" data-line=\"419\">419</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"2\" data-line=\"102\">Il. 2.102</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"3\" data-line=\"104\">Il. 3.104</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"4\" data-line=\"23\">Il. 4.23, etc</a>.: <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"4\" data-line=\"472\">Od. 4.472</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"7\" data-line=\"164\">Od. 7.164</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"8\" data-line=\"432\">Od. 8.432, etc</a>. Acc. Δία <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"1\" data-line=\"394\">394</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"2\" data-line=\"2\">Il. 2.2</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"5\" data-line=\"419\">Il. 5.419, etc</a>. : <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"14\" data-line=\"389\">Od. 14.389</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"14\" data-line=\"406\">406</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"20\" data-line=\"75\">Od. 20.75</a>. Διόθεν [&amp;gt;-θεν], from Zeus <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"24\" data-line=\"194\">Il. 24.194</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"24\" data-line=\"561\">561</a>. By his power or will <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"15\" data-line=\"489\">Il. 15.489</a>. (ἀθάνατος, αἰγίοχος , ἄναξ, ἀργικέραυνος , ἄριστος, ἀστεροπητής , ἐριβρεμέτης, ἐρίγδουπος , ἐρισθενής, εὐρύοπα , Ἰδαῖος, ἱκετήσιος , καταχθόνιος, κελαινεφής , κρείων, κύδιστος , μέγας, μέγιστος, Ἴδηθεν (Δωδώνης) μεδέων, μητίετα, αἰθέρι ( τηλόθι) ναίων, νεφεληγερέτα, ξείνιος, ξένιος, Ὀλύμπιος, πανομφαῖος, πατήρ, π. ἀνδρῶν τε θεῶν τε , στεροπηγερέτα, τελεσφόρος , τερπικέραυνος, ὕπατος , ὕ. κρειόντων, ὑπερμενής , ὑψιβρεμέτης, ὑψίζυγος , ὑψόθ&#x27; ἐών.) Patronymic Κρονίδης, Κρονίων. The supreme god, son of Cronus and Rhea, brother of Poseidon, Hades, Hera and Demeter, and husband (and brother) of Hera. Father (1) by Hera of Ares, Hebe and Hephaestus; (2) by Leto of Apollo and Artemis; (3) by Dione of Aphrodite; (4) by Semele of Dionysus; (5) by Maia of Hermes; (6) by Demeter of Persephoneia; (7) by Europa (daughter of Phoenix-2) of Minos and Rhadamanthys; (8) by Leda of Helen; (9) by Alcmene of Heracles; (10) by Laodameia of Sarpedon; (11) by Danae of Perseus-1; (12) by Antiope of Amphion-2 and Zethus; (13) by Dia of Peirithous; and (14) by unnamed mothers of Athene , Dardanus-1, Aeacus and Tantalus. Father also of Ate <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"19\" data-line=\"91\">Il. 19.91</a>; of the river Xanthus-1 <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"14\" data-line=\"434\">Il. 14.434</a>; of the Muses <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"2\" data-line=\"491\">Il. 2.491</a> , <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"2\" data-line=\"598\">598</a>: <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"8\" data-line=\"488\">Od. 8.488</a>; of nymphs <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"6\" data-line=\"420\">Il. 6.420</a>: <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"6\" data-line=\"105\">Od. 6.105</a> , <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"9\" data-line=\"154\">Od. 9.154</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"13\" data-line=\"356\">Od. 13.356</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"17\" data-line=\"240\">Od. 17.240</a>; of Λιταί <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"9\" data-line=\"502\">502</a>. Protector of heralds. See under κῆρυξ in Lex. And of strangers, beggars and suppliants <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"6\" data-line=\"207\">Od. 6.207</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"9\" data-line=\"270\">Od. 9.270, etc</a>. See also ξείνιος 1, ξένιος 2 in Lex. His scales. See τάλαντον 1 in Lex. His thunderbolts <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"8\" data-line=\"133\">Il. 8.133</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"21\" data-line=\"198\">Il. 21.198, etc</a>.: <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"5\" data-line=\"128\">Od. 5.128</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"12\" data-line=\"415\">Od. 12.415, etc</a>. Sender of rain <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"12\" data-line=\"25\">Il. 12.25, etc</a>.: <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"9\" data-line=\"111\">Od. 9.111, etc</a>. Of snow <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"10\" data-line=\"5\">Il. 10.5</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"12\" data-line=\"279\">Il. 12.279</a> , <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"19\" data-line=\"357\">Il. 19.357</a>. Of winds <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"12\" data-line=\"252\">Il. 12.252</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"13\" data-line=\"795\">Il. 13.795, etc</a>. : <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"9\" data-line=\"67\">Od. 9.67</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"15\" data-line=\"297\">Od. 15.297, etc</a>. And of the rainbow <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"11\" data-line=\"27\">Il. 11.27</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"17\" data-line=\"547\">Il. 17.547</a>. By lot (<a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"15\" data-line=\"187\">Il. 15.187</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"15\" data-line=\"192\">192) got the heavens and the upper air as his realm (but he is called</a> καταχθόνιος <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"9\" data-line=\"457\">457)</a>. The attempt of Hera, Athene and Poseidon to put him in bonds <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"1\" data-line=\"399\">Il. 1.399</a>; Thetis goes to him on behalf of Achilles <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"1\" data-line=\"493\">Il. 1.493</a>, his promise to her <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"1\" data-line=\"518\">518</a>; sends Oneirus to beguile Agamemnon <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"2\" data-line=\"8\">Il. 2.8</a>; sends Athene to induce the Trojans to break the truce <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"4\" data-line=\"70\">Il. 4.70</a>; with threats forbids the assembled gods to help either side <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"8\" data-line=\"1\">Il. 8.1</a>; sends a thunderbolt which falls before the chariot of Diomedes <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"8\" data-line=\"133\">Il. 8.133</a>; sends an omen to comfort Agamemnon <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"8\" data-line=\"247\">Il. 8.247</a>; sends Iris to turn back Hera and Athene <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"8\" data-line=\"399\">Il. 8.399</a>; sends Eris to encourage the Greeks <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"11\" data-line=\"3\">Il. 11.3</a>; sends Iris to Hector with advice <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"11\" data-line=\"185\">Il. 11.185</a>; beguiled and lulled to sleep by Hera <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"14\" data-line=\"292\">Il. 14.292</a>, his rage when he awakes <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"15\" data-line=\"4\">Il. 15.4</a>; summons Iris and Apollo <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"15\" data-line=\"54\">Il. 15.54</a>, sends her to bid Poseidon retire from the fight <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"15\" data-line=\"158\">158</a>, and him to aid Hector <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"15\" data-line=\"221\">221</a>; debates with himself as to Sarpedon&#x27;s fate <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"16\" data-line=\"433\">Il. 16.433</a>, resolves on his death <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"16\" data-line=\"458\">458</a>, charges Apollo with his funeral rites <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"16\" data-line=\"667\">667</a>; Hera tricked him in the matter of the birth of Heracles <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"19\" data-line=\"95\">Il. 19.95</a>, his rage thereat <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"19\" data-line=\"125\">125</a>; sends Athene to comfort Achilles <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"19\" data-line=\"342\">Il. 19.342</a> ; summons an assembly of the gods <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"20\" data-line=\"4\">Il. 20.4</a>, allows the gods to take sides in the fight <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"20\" data-line=\"20\">20</a>; pities Hector&#x27;s plight <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"22\" data-line=\"168\">Il. 22.168, but allows</a> Athene to go to the assistance of Achilles <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"22\" data-line=\"183\">183</a>; sends Thetis to Achilles to induce him to give up Hector&#x27;s corpse <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"24\" data-line=\"104\">Il. 24.104</a> , and Iris to Priam to bid him go to the ships and ransom the corpse <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"24\" data-line=\"144\">144</a> , sends Hermes to aid <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"17\" data-line=\"334\">Il. 17.334, etc. : speaks of</a> Aegisthus to the assembled gods <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"1\" data-line=\"31\">Od. 1.31</a>; sends an eagle as a good omen to Telemachus <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"2\" data-line=\"146\">Od. 2.146</a>; sends Hermes to bid Calypso let Odysseus go <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"5\" data-line=\"29\">Od. 5.29</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"7\" data-line=\"261\">Od. 7.261</a>; thunders as a good sign to Odysseus <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"20\" data-line=\"103\">Od. 20.103</a>; gives his voice for peace between Odysseus and his people <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"24\" data-line=\"478\">Od. 24.478, and sends a thunderbolt to stop the fighting</a> <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"24\" data-line=\"539\">539</a>; etc.</div>", "src": "hompers"}, "zugo/n": {"key": "zugo/n", "head": "ζυγόν", "html": "<div class=\"cunliffe-sense\">ζυγόν -οῦ, τό [cf. L. jugum, Eng. yoke.] Ablative ζυγόφι(ν) Il. 19.404, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"24\" data-line=\"576\">Il. 24.576</a>. 1 A yoke for draught-animals <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"5\" data-line=\"730\">Il. 5.730</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"5\" data-line=\"731\">731</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"8\" data-line=\"543\">Il. 8.543</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"16\" data-line=\"470\">Il. 16.470</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"24\" data-line=\"268\">Il. 24.268, etc</a>.: <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"3\" data-line=\"383\">Od. 3.383</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"3\" data-line=\"486\">486 =</a> <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"15\" data-line=\"184\">Od. 15.184</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"4\" data-line=\"39\">Od. 4.39</a>. 2 In pl., oarsmen&#x27;s benches extending from side to side of a ship: ὑπὸ ζυγὰ δῆσα [ἑτάρους] Od. 9.99. Cf. <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"13\" data-line=\"21\">Od. 13.21</a>. 3 The cross-bar which joined the horns of a lyre and to which the strings were fastened <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"9\" data-line=\"187\">Il. 9.187</a>.</div>", "src": "lex"}, "zah/s": {"key": "zah/s", "head": "ζαής", "html": "<div class=\"cunliffe-sense\">ζαής [ζα- + ἠ-, ἄημι.] Acc. ζαῆν <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"12\" data-line=\"313\">Od. 12.313</a>. Blowing strongly, furious, blustering <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"12\" data-line=\"157\">Il. 12.157</a>: <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"5\" data-line=\"368\">Od. 5.368</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"12\" data-line=\"313\">Od. 12.313</a>.</div>", "src": "lex"}, "zhte/w": {"key": "zhte/w", "head": "ζητέω", "html": "<div class=\"cunliffe-sense\">ζητέω [cf. δίζημαι, δίζω.] To seek, seek for: ἔμʼ ἔξοχα πάντων ζήτει <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"14\" data-line=\"258\">Il. 14.258</a>.</div>", "src": "lex"}, "zaflegh/s": {"key": "zaflegh/s", "head": "ζαφλεγής", "html": "<div class=\"cunliffe-sense\">ζαφλεγής [ζα- + φλέγω.] Full of fire or life. Of men <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"21\" data-line=\"465\">Il. 21.465</a>.</div>", "src": "lex"}, "za/qeos": {"key": "za/qeos", "head": "ζάθεος", "html": "<div class=\"cunliffe-sense\">ζάθεος -η [ζα- + θεῖος.] Holy, sacred. Like ἠγάθεος, epithet of places<a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"1\" data-line=\"38\">Il. 1.38 =</a> <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"1\" data-line=\"452\">452</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"2\" data-line=\"508\">Il. 2.508</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"2\" data-line=\"520\">520</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"9\" data-line=\"151\">Il. 9.151 =</a> <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"9\" data-line=\"293\">293</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"15\" data-line=\"432\">Il. 15.432</a>.</div>", "src": "lex"}, "zwgre/w": {"key": "zwgre/w", "head": "ζωγρέω1", "html": "<div class=\"cunliffe-sense\">ζωγρέω1 [ζωός + ἀγρέω.] To take alive, spare a prisoner&#x27;s life <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"6\" data-line=\"46\">Il. 6.46 =</a> <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"11\" data-line=\"131\">Il. 11.131</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"10\" data-line=\"378\">Il. 10.378</a>.</div><div class=\"cunliffe-sense\">ζωγρέω2 [ζωή + ἀγείρω or ἐγείρω.] To re-assemble or rouse the vital forces of, revive <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"5\" data-line=\"698\">Il. 5.698</a>.</div>", "src": "lex"}, "ze/leia": {"key": "ze/leia", "head": "Ζέλεια", "html": "<div class=\"cunliffe-sense\">Ζέλεια (ἱερή). A town of the Troad on the Aesepus-1 <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"2\" data-line=\"824\">Il. 2.824</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"4\" data-line=\"103\">Il. 4.103</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"4\" data-line=\"121\">121</a>.</div>", "src": "hompers"}, "zei/dwros": {"key": "zei/dwros", "head": "ζείδωρος", "html": "<div class=\"cunliffe-sense\">ζείδωρος -ον [ζειαί + δωρέομαι.] Grain-giving. Epithet of the earth <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"2\" data-line=\"548\">Il. 2.548</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"8\" data-line=\"486\">Il. 8.486</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"20\" data-line=\"226\">Il. 20.226</a>: <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"3\" data-line=\"3\">Od. 3.3 =</a> <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"12\" data-line=\"386\">Od. 12.386</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"4\" data-line=\"229\">Od. 4.229</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"5\" data-line=\"463\">Od. 5.463</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"7\" data-line=\"332\">Od. 7.332</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"9\" data-line=\"357\">Od. 9.357</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"11\" data-line=\"309\">Od. 11.309</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"13\" data-line=\"354\">Od. 13.354</a>, <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"19\" data-line=\"593\">Od. 19.593</a>.</div>", "src": "lex"}, "za/kotos": {"key": "za/kotos", "head": "ζάκοτος", "html": "<div class=\"cunliffe-sense\">ζάκοτος [ζα- + κότος.] Surly, cross-grained. Absol. <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"iliad\" data-book=\"3\" data-line=\"220\">Il. 3.220</a>.</div>", "src": "lex"}, "zefuri/h": {"key": "zefuri/h", "head": "Ζεφυρίη", "html": "<div class=\"cunliffe-sense\">Ζεφυρίη ἡ [fem. of adj. fr. Ζέφυρος.] = Ζέφυρος. <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"7\" data-line=\"119\">Od. 7.119</a>.</div>", "src": "lex"}, "zh=qos": {"key": "zh=qos", "head": "Ζῆθος", "html": "<div class=\"cunliffe-sense\">Ζῆθος (ἄναξ). Son of Zeus and Antiope. With his brother Amphion-2 represented as having founded Thebes-1 <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"11\" data-line=\"262\">Od. 11.262</a>; <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"19\" data-line=\"523\">Od. 19.523 (see also</a> Πανδάρεος).</div>", "src": "hompers"}, "zhlh/mwn": {"key": "zhlh/mwn", "head": "ζηλήμων", "html": "<div class=\"cunliffe-sense\">ζηλήμων -ονος [ζῆλος, jealousy.] Jealous, envious: σχέτλιοί ἐστε, θεοί, ζηλήμονες <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"5\" data-line=\"118\">Od. 5.118</a>.</div>", "src": "lex"}, "zw=stron": {"key": "zw=stron", "head": "ζῶστρον", "html": "<div class=\"cunliffe-sense\">ζῶστρον τό [as ζωστήρ.] = ζωστήρ. (2) <a class=\"cunliffe-cite\" href=\"#\" data-work=\"odyssey\" data-book=\"6\" data-line=\"38\">Od. 6.38</a>.</div>", "src": "lex"}}